// from buoyancy_compare_box_r1_mem_gas.prm (edit that file or the script): identical except
// initialTiltAngleDeg 25 about world Y on the FloatingBox.
//
// MEM vs analytical buoyancy, MEM arm, resolution level R = 1: a fully submerged box (halfExtents 8 = 8R,
// densityRatio 0.5) rises through still water (targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0).
// useMemOnlyBuoyancy true and useBognerThreePhaseMEM true (project defaults, set explicitly; they must be switched
// together): buoyancy comes from the MEM force alone, no analytic term.
// Tilt 25 deg: upright, the box faces pass through cell centres (mapping tie) and the bottom layer can map flush onto
// the floor with no fluid cell below it, which starves MEM buoyancy of the pressure from below. Both arms are
// tilted so that they start from the same state.
//
// Domain and floater scale with R, the physical scenario is the same for every R. Domain <48,48,96>, cellsPerBlock
// <16,16,12> -> 3x3x8 = 72 processes (1 node).
// Periodic in x and y (one floater; cross-section ~3x the floater size, the minimum without self-image
// interaction), no-slip T/B. liquidHeightFactor 6 (production value 2.862) for a deep liquid column. Box centre
// <24,24,41.5>: domain centre in x and y, z = floorHeight (floorHeightFactor x avg diameter; no bed, liquid down to the
// bottom wall) + ~1.05 half-extents.
// Units: inFileName is the bed generated by BedGeneration_buoyancy_r1.prm; avgParticleDiameter and dx_SI are read
// from it (getAvgDiameterScalingFactor, Utility.h), no override; avg diameter_SI 0.00289997651976604 at every R.
// gravityOverride = 9.81*dt_SI^2/dx_SI with dt_SI = nu_LU/nu_SI*dx_SI^2, nu_LU = 0.000214026 (useHardcodedUnits).
// timesteps: 2600 at R = 1, about 70% of the step (~3790) at which the floater top reached the waterline in an
// R = 1 calibration run; scaled by R^2 for R = 2, 4 (dt_SI ~ 1/R^2, same physical time). The log's subm= field
// cannot detect such a breach in either arm; check pos.z against the waterline height instead.

